AgriTrust Project Summary

Project Name: AgriTrust
Project Type: Smart agriculture decision support and direct farmer-to-buyer marketplace
Technology: Python, Flask, SQLAlchemy, MySQL/SQLite, OpenCV, NumPy, Pillow, TensorFlow-ready AI, Chart.js

1. Overview
AgriTrust is a production-style agriculture platform that helps farmers manage farms, track crop growth, analyze soil and crop health, make better agronomic decisions, and sell produce directly to buyers. It reduces dependence on intermediaries, improves farm trust, and supports better crop planning and supply chain visibility.

The system combines decision support, image-based disease assessment, market access, future harvest reservations, and trust-building analytics in one platform.

2. System Architecture
Client (Browser) -> Flask Web App -> Blueprints/Routes -> SQLAlchemy Models -> MySQL or SQLite Database
                -> Uploads folder for images
                -> AI / OpenCV image processing
                -> Weather and agronomy advisory services

The app is organized into modules for:
- Authentication
- Dashboard
- Farms
- Crops
- Recommendations
- Disease detection
- Chatbot
- Weather advisory
- Marketplace
- Reservations
- Orders
- Analytics
- Traceability
- Admin

3. Main Features
- User authentication with role-based access control for FARMER, BUYER, and ADMIN
- Farmer dashboard with daily tasks, crop cards, revenue summaries, and charts
- Farm management with acreage, soil type, irrigation type, and location info
- Crop lifecycle tracking from planting to harvest readiness
- Crop recommendation engine based on weather, soil, location, season, acreage, and water availability
- Crop disease detection using image uploads and OpenCV preprocessing
- AI monitoring and agronomy guidance for disease conditions and treatment recommendations
- Smart farming guide for major crops such as tomato, rice, banana, and cucumber
- AI chatbot assistant for farm and marketplace support
- Weather advisory integration with OpenWeatherMap-style guidance
- Direct marketplace with product listings, filters, stock visibility, and buyer orders
- Future harvest reservation workflow
- Harvest batch and quality traceability with unique batch IDs
- Trust profile calculation for farmers based on completed orders, verified batches, and buyer feedback
- Revenue analytics and waste reduction insights
- Admin moderation and verification controls

4. Technology Stack
Backend:
- Python
- Flask
- Flask-SQLAlchemy
- PyMySQL
- python-dotenv
- Werkzeug
- Jinja2
- requests

AI and computer vision:
- OpenCV
- NumPy
- Pillow
- TensorFlow / Keras (optional model integration)

Frontend:
- HTML5
- CSS3
- JavaScript
- Chart.js
- Jinja2 templates

Database:
- MySQL (preferred)
- SQLite fallback for local / demo use

5. Database and Configuration
The project uses configuration variables from config.py and optional environment variables through .env.
Main settings include:
- SECRET_KEY
- DB_USER
- DB_PASSWORD
- DB_HOST
- DB_PORT
- DB_NAME
- USE_SQLITE_FALLBACK
- WEATHER_API_KEY
- AI_API_KEY
- DISEASE_MODEL_PATH

The app automatically creates upload directories and initializes tables. If MySQL is unavailable, it falls back to an SQLite database automatically.

